    "setLabel": "7.3 Eg.7",
    "stem": "Find \\(\\int \\sin 2x \\cos 3x\\,dx\\).",
    "solution": "Recall the identity \\(\\sin x \\cos y = \\dfrac{1}{2}[\\sin (x+y) + \\sin (x-y)]\\). Then \\(\\int \\sin 2x \\cos 3x\\,dx = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[\\int \\sin 5x\\,dx - \\int \\sin x\\,dx\\right] = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[-\\dfrac{1}{5}\\cos 5x + \\cos x\\right] + C = -\\dfrac{1}{10}\\cos 5x + \\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos x + C\\)."
